Well, Samurais are, like, Samurais. They cut things into tiny
slices, unless they're stickin' 'em full of *ya*s from a
distance.

Pretty ok early game, Minetown was relatively deep, and in
that annoying Grotto version. That was compensated for by a
coaligned temple and some nice stuff: pre-blessed magic lamp,
Hawaiian shirt, BoH, and an incredible +5 pair of iron shoes.

Switched from katana to Snickersnee+katana.

Dlvl:4 had a general shop with another magic lamp. The wish
went on a CoMR.

Found my first long sword, and switched to Excalibur+katana at
the Oracle.

Smokies were acid. Doesn't get any nastier than that. I've
seen something like four of them in the entire game, and
didn't get any wishes out of them (well, I've actually seen a
LOT more, but usually just before they crashed on my
forehead).

Hard time finding clear potions (I hadn't seen any at that
point in the game), but a wand of cancellation helped.

Even harder time identifying stuff - my first full inventory
id came at Clvl:18/Dlvl:17. And not because I haven't tried.

Unfortunately, Soko had another BoH.

Mine's End - Catacombs again. Got crowned there (I'm playing
3.4.0, and crowning is possible there even when not standing
at an altar). Damn.

My first Big Cave - Oval-shaped one. Easy, even though I fell
through a trap door, and had to fight away from the stairs.

Altar at Dlvl:14, coaligned temple at Dlvl:17.

Visited the Quest, looted those storerooms. Crap. But a trio
of samurais left behind a couple of AoLS. Guess they didn't
have any time to eqiup those. Sort of Boris Akunin-style:
"Master, let's attack and slay those samurais before they
could prepare for battle!"

Found Fort Ludios, and experienced an extremely stupid and
annoying death, choking on some poor leprechaun. Good thing I
had one of those AoLS on. But should've been wearing an amulet
of magical breathing anyway. I just didn't think I would choke
and die - I didn't remember eating anything recently enough,
but I still didn't get the warning.

Medusa (Central Island): another case of extreme stupidity.
Killed a coupl'a giants, and while munching on their bodies
saw a black dragon approaching. Now I don't know what in seven
hells I was thinking, but I barely escaped without my CoMR and
dwarven mithril coat.

Obviously, I couldn't take on that dragon without reflection,
and, obviously, living without magic resistance is nigh
impossible. And I only had one wish (that aforementioned magic
lamp). Well, wished for a magic marker and reverse genocided
silver dragons. Risky, only the last (fifth) one dropped the
scales. I've lost heaps of AC, and it only got worse when I
angered the priest by killing a gas spore next to him.

I've only seen two floating eyes after that, and neither
dropped a corpse (btw, this time I've got telepathy from
praying, not from one of them... Amaterasu Omikami giveth and
Amaterasu Omikami taketh away...)

Also, that reverse genocide was the only one in the game - I
haven't seen any potions of unholy water, and that was my only
cursed scroll of blank paper. All the HPs come from alchemy.

Being reckless with magical breathing around Medusa's costed
me some more stuff, but nothing really good.

Well, somehow I got to the Castle without dying. The only
useful thing in the storerooms was a helm of brilliance. WoW
was at (0:1): another CoMR, speed boots, ring of free action
and magic markers.

I've found a wand of death somewhere, so I took on the Quest.

Ashikaga Takauji fell to a single *zzzZZZTTTttt*. So buddy,
now you know what a *real* instakill looks like. Gehennom was
relatively easy, and the only demon prince who gave me trouble
was Baalzebub. This time he was bent on escaping downwards,
though (wand of digging).

At this point I had expertise in #twoweapon, long swords
(milked Amaterasu Omikami for the Frost Brand), two-handed
swords and bows. Skilled in clerical spells, basic knowledge
of knives and shurikens (never found enough of the latter to
advance any further). Stopped using SoIDs, could do with the
spell.

During another sacrificial orgy a xorn dropped a WoW. (0:1),
too, but I was more than happy with that. Non-magical lamps
lasted me almost all of Gehennom, and those few wishes allowed
me to finalize the character.

Prepared for the final run, and made an incredibly stupid
mistake just before breaching Wizard Tower's wall - stepped
into the moat, losing all of my c?oTeleports (and nothing
else).

I had a WoW (1:1) stashed away in my bag, so I wished for a
magic marker and wrote on those cursed blank scrolls.

Killed Rodney on turn 66666.

Moloch's Sanctum was easy again - conflict truly rocks there.

But the mysterious force on the way back to surface was, for
once, incredibly annoying. I've seen the top of the Tower six
times, Orcus' Town six times, Baalzebub's Lair five times, and
Juiblex' Swamp four times. I guess that's some sort of
national record. I've never had nearly as much trouble with
it before.

Elemental Planes - easy, even air elementals weren't tough
enough for me.

But Astral was hell. I've got some real taste of Pestilence
for the first time, too, - I've never respected the guy
before, but now I'm definitely going to. Absence of telepathy
was extremely displeasing, - I've never realized just how much
time you spend on Astral being blind. I even switched to AoESP
instead of AoLS, although that was risky. I had to fight all
three Riders for the first time, and even conflict didn't help
a lot.

But in the end, I prevailed. Standing on the lawful altar I
uncursed my stuff, quaffed PoFHs, and sacrificed the Amulet.

